  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "none",
    "relation": "discusses",
    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The study compares downstream benchmark scores for NVLM-X models of two sizes, a different measurement from the claimed pretraining-loss scaling laws.",
    "gate_note": "The study does not measure held-out pretraining cross-entropy, fit power laws, test extrapolation from smaller runs, or measure compute-optimal allocations. The rows record the matched 34B-to-72B downstream benchmark comparisons in Table 9, which bear on V6. Other benchmark results and ablations do not provide a matched model-size comparison for this version.",
    "test_reason": "This is a model-building report for NVLM 1.0. It does not test the claim. Its only size comparison (Table 9, NVLM-X 34B vs 72B) changes the backbone LLM along with size (Nous-Hermes-2-Yi-34B vs Qwen2-72B-Instruct). It also uses different SFT hyperparameters (Table 11), and the authors say the 34B models were left unoptimized. These are two points with no fitted trend and no loss measurement. The authors' remark that 'accuracy scales well' from 34B to 72B is an aside, not a result on scaling predictability.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Mostly right, but it overweights a side remark. The paper's main conclusions concern architecture (decoder-only vs cross-attention vs hybrid), 1-D tile tags for high-resolution input, data quality over scale, and preserving or improving text-only performance through high-quality text SFT data. The 34B→72B 'scales well' remark appears only in the frozen-vs-unfrozen subsection. That subsection also notes the frozen 72B performs only comparably to the unfrozen 34B.",
    "recipe": "none",
    "recipe_differences": "The study evaluates multimodal benchmark performance across two model sizes; it does not apply a language-model pretraining-loss scaling-law procedure.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Model size (34B versus 72B) and whether the LLM backbone is frozen during multimodal SFT are varied.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "NVLM-X built on Qwen2-72B outperforms NVLM-X built on Yi-34B on all nine VL benchmarks, frozen and unfrozen (Table 9). The two models differ in backbone family as well as size.",
        "proposed_claim": "Swapping in a larger, stronger backbone LLM improves multimodal benchmark scores of cross-attention VLMs.",
